{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":2,"query":"name=Housel&limit=10&title=The Psychology of Money","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"psychology of money ","subTitle":"timeless lessons on wealth, greed, and happiness "},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Timeless lessons on wealth, greed, and happiness"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Housel, Morgan","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjJHmC4GWTC7pMJtqMfC8K"},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"still image"},{"@authority":"Library of Congress Subject Headings","#text":"Short stories."},{"@authority":"Medical Subject Headings","#text":"Anecdotes"},{"@authority":"aat","#text":"short stories."},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Anecdotes"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Short stories"},{"@authority":"gsafd","#text":"Short stories"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Short stories"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Anecdotes"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Nouvelles."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Anecdotes."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"xxk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"United Kingdom"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2020"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2020"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Great Britain, United Kingdom :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Harriman House,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2020."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"x, 242 pages : illustrations ; 23 cm"},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Doing well with money isn't necessarily about what you know. It's about how you behave. And behavior is hard to teach, even to really smart people. Money--investing, personal finance, and business decisions--is typically taught as a math-based field, where data and formulas tell us exactly what to do. But in the real world people don't make financial decisions on a spreadsheet. They make them at the dinner table, or in a meeting room, where personal history, your own unique view of the world, ego, pride, marketing, and odd incentives are scrambled together. In The Psychology of Money, award-winning author Morgan Housel shares 19 short stories exploring the strange ways people think about money and teaches you how to make better sense of one of life's most important topics.--Publisher's description"},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"No one's crazy -- Luck & risk -- Never enough -- Confounding compounding -- Getting wealthy vs. staying wealthy -- Tails, you win -- Freedom -- Man in the car paradox -- Wealth is what you don't see -- Save money -- Reasonable > rational -- Surprise! -- Room for error -- You'll change -- Nothing's free -- You & me -- The seduction of pessimism -- When you'll believe anything -- All together now -- Confessions -- Postscript: A brief history of why the U.S. consumer thinks the way they do."},"targetAudience":{"@authority":"marctarget","#text":"adult"},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Morgan Housel."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Money","Psychological aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh",